{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/40074-what-does-stygia-look-like","id":40074,"title":"What Does Stygia Look Like?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-31T11:29:22-08:00","id":40074,"title":"What Does Stygia Look Like?","content":"What does Stygia look like to you, in your mind? To me it resembles Manhattan, with a very similar geography and a look that is a cross between the works of Jacek Yerka, <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">MC Escher and H. Bosch if they were trying to depict &quot;modern&quot; New York City.<br /> <br /> But what does it look like to you?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T13:22:49-08:00","id":40128,"title":"","content":"It began in the time of Rome and saw a massive population influx with the Black Plague, so I see those as the primary infuences on the architecture, albeit stacked on top of each other higher than ever possible in life. Stygia has taken in European dead for hundreds of years, so you get all sorts of styles. MC Escher meets the great cities of Europe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T13:55:40-08:00","id":40142,"title":"","content":"Well I've always pictured Stygia as this huge, sprawling metropolis centered around the Onyx Tower. Of course the buildings themselves are a miss-mash of structures from different time periods, ranging from the Roman Empire to today as well as buildings that are truly alien or at least never seen on Earth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T16:59:24-08:00","id":40229,"title":"","content":"I played <i>Earthdawn</i> before I discovered the cWoD, so my version always looked a lot like Thera from that game. Basically, a massive island (I guess Manhattan could work, but more circular and bigger), only in this case it's got all sorts of buildings that don't work together architecturally. (Like the World Trade Center towers across the park from the library of Alexandria).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/426-big-brother","name":"Big Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T17:29:47-08:00","id":40252,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">We used specific descriptions for specific buildings, but the phrase I often used to describe the vibe of Stygia\u2019s architectural mojo was, </span><i>\u201c\u2026if Romans, Normans, and the Holy Roman Empire designed the cities of Manhattan, LA, and Chicago then smooshed them all on top of each other.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">Nowadays, I might be tempted (if given the opportunity)to come up with a more nuanced description. At the time, however, it conveyed the right sense of monolithically-metropolitan gothic aesthetics that I imagined the city to possess.</span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T17:30:17-08:00","id":40253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Big Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/40074-what-does-stygia-look-like?p=40229#post40229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Like the World Trade Center towers across the park from the library of Alexandria).</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me love you. I never considered the actual specific buildings that would show up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T21:34:30-08:00","id":40344,"title":"","content":"Hrm... If the Last Grgeat Maelstrom has not happened yet in Wr20, then the World Trade Center Towers probably would be in the Shadowlands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T22:17:43-08:00","id":40356,"title":"","content":"Yeah they would be right there in the Shadowlands version of New York City. Though I suppose that given the nature of their destruction it is possible that one or both of the towers could have been pushed deeper into the Underworld, ending up within Stygia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T23:08:54-08:00","id":40932,"title":"","content":"I always pictured The Necropolis as a worse version of a city in an Alex Proyas film ala The Crow or Dark City. Nowadays I picture something more along the lines of a bastardized Inception setting inside of Silent Hill's &quot;Otherworld&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T07:28:41-08:00","id":41100,"title":"","content":"I've always imagined Stygia as looking mostly like Tim Burton getting his hands on a book of famous leveled architecture and then making a collage out of the pictures.<br /> <br /> Or maybe if Dr Seuss and Vincent Van Gogh collaborated on a series of landscapes (Ted for the style, Vince for the dark and crazy edge).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T20:47:27-08:00","id":41490,"title":"","content":"I'd say the town gets more older and rundown the further in it . In general most of it is a mishmash of destroyed buildings and the like","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1268-cosmic-mind","name":"Cosmic Mind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1268_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T21:10:07-08:00","id":45367,"title":"","content":"Funny Enough, i 